    "loudest_elsewhere": [],
    "why": "The channel every figure in this record was read from, and the highest each channel of the interface reached across the takes this record was built from. Chosen once for the run rather than per take: the interface carries inputs the unit is not on, those inputs are not silent, and a take whose output falls below one of them is read from that input instead -- which returns a level, and a rate, belonging to something else. `loudest_elsewhere` names every take whose own loudest channel is not the one used, because a reading that changed channel is exactly what the figures cannot say on their own."
